    "body": "Closes #133.\n\nImplements ADR-017: `display: none` works, and the hardcoded skip list in `layout.cpp` is retired. The skip decision moves from C++ to the cascade, where CSS 2.1 specifies it belongs.\n\n## The gap this fixes\n\nSince PR #110, `layout.cpp` had a hardcoded helper that skipped 7 tags during layout: `head`, `style`, `script`, `title`, `meta`, `link`, `base`. It worked, but:\n\n- **Not overridable by author CSS.** `<head style=\"display: block\">` could not render.\n- **Magic special case.** Future contributors had to learn about this list before touching `layout_element`.\n- **Redundant with the `Display` enum.** ADR-016 added `Display::None` but never wired it in.\n\n## What changed\n\n**`ua_stylesheet.cpp`**: 8 rules added.\n\n    head, style, script, title, meta, link, base, template { display: none }\n\n`template` is added beyond the old skip list because per HTML5 it does not render.\n\n**`layout.cpp`**: delete `is_non_rendered_tag`, add `display_of(child_style) == Display::None` check in the block-child iteration path.\n\n**`tests/test_ua_stylesheet.cpp`**: rule count 14 -> 15.\n\n**`tests/test_layout.cpp`**: 4 new tests, plus a `run_with_ua` helper for tests that need UA defaults.\n\n## Two behavior changes\n\n**Author override now works.** `<head style=\"display: block\">` renders. Before, the C++ helper pre-empted any author CSS.\n\n**Author `display:none` works for any element.** `div { display: none }` in author CSS now skips the div. Before, only 7 hardcoded tags could be skipped.\n\n## Tests\n\n- 217 cases, 852 assertions, all pass (was 213/839 on main)\n- 4 new `[layout][display_none]` tests\n- 3 existing `[layout][skip]` tests updated to use `run_with_ua` so they exercise the UA stylesheet path\n\n## What this unlocks\n\nFuture \"this element doesn't render\" cases become UA stylesheet changes, not C++ changes. Candidates for later:\n- `<noscript>` when scripts are disabled\n- `<dialog>` without `[open]` (needs pseudo-class support, deferred)\n- `<option>` outside a `<select>` (needs form-element layout, deferred)\n\n## Deferred\n\n- `display: flex`, `grid`, `table`, `contents` -- different layout modes\n- `visibility: hidden` -- occupies space, just invisible\n- `@media`-conditional `display: none` -- at-rules deferred\n\n## Next\n\nWith ADR-017 landed, `layout.cpp` has no hardcoded tag lists. The pipeline is driven entirely by cascade + UA stylesheet + box model. Next natural ADRs: pseudo-classes (`:hover`, `:link`), `@media` queries, or `display: flex`.\n",
